"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e643aa2a5baad483db6dda5636a96d95cf428a3614ecfe2ee1e687ca961e51d","compact":"37305c49967b72781e2dc73362d7e018ebe8a42ef8f91ccbe98dcda873b75dfe","nasal":"0adf1e84d7d2cda4154474c6acd73bc173a9f6c2378931b9aa6bf5f2e98625cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":18,"english":"And he smote Death with four, the (Yama's), charioteer with seven, and swiftly struck Yama in the marrow with hundreds and thousands of shafts. :","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.766,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fdaa3c014a7924ce35ed0ef271c45ad000bdb4339f12f839290ff5c84d2e1b82","compact":"938c88938b36f0c5ceea075aad5f9d8d05b82e823807b427819ea671c6ccb0f8","nasal":"938c88938b36f0c5ceea075aad5f9d8d05b82e823807b427819ea671c6ccb0f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":19,"english":"Then from forth Yama's mouth there issued darted flames with his teeth mixed with smoke, the fire of his fury.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.127,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d67c33161ec4bddb9c5f4b53dd338df8e7e97f8724d0b66f0a31f564bfe67f9","compact":"f98ad262f3cbbea281a8acb2e6ca96c7b0c834c2e7e8251b862dd76acf9b58f7","nasal":"f98ad262f3cbbea281a8acb2e6ca96c7b0c834c2e7e8251b862dd76acf9b58f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":20,"english":"Having entered there without any councillor the vicious Rāvana, the lord of Räkşasas, on beholding that chaste damsel with sweet smiles seated on a royal seat, being possessed by desire, grew anxious to hold her by the hand, as one, under the influence of death, catches a sleeping serpent. Beholding that lord of Rākşasas with loose cloth and understanding him as desirous of holding (her) the deity, having huge arms, asleep and enveloped with flames, laughed aloud. And searched suddenly by his energy, Ravana, the dread of all people, fell down on earth like to an up-rooted tree. Beholding that Raksasa fallen he said the following words: “Rise up, O foremost of Raksasas, you shall not meet with death today; you shall live and be protected, O Raksasa, by the great Patriarch's boon. Do you therefore go away, O Ravana, with confidence, you shall not experience death just now.\"","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.452,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-113"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"984801352dddb5124e355e91d2346062da78d940f53a5799479111b7846dc55d","compact":"d0f733ff251a28ffe19fcc43bc3f08134c9ab585a628d125c56c24c0a95ba44a","nasal":"9328740f2bc369ec566efb0d1c70d4464f023e6977035bd7d5bbc5bbcdcdf505"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":21,"english":"And beholding a Rși there he said to him, “Welcome you are, O celestial saint. Indeed you have come at a proper season. Who is this shameless Wight that is going is seated on a car and attended by Apsarās? Does he not perceive his object of fear?\" Being thus addressed by Ravana, Parvata said, \"O my child, O you gifted with great intellect, Hear I shall describe to you the truth.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.46,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-83"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9a87fb73fbccb65ef590016e888195fbecb9c5eedd5f3cb55067f661746f4de2","compact":"51ca8f58aa635ce0eb49882686f215e4a43f2f8aa7d54312fd0d1805410f7ec1","nasal":"f6d406025ffe6505d3f954777fd6ba063f8fb41d5900c16c338297f401a1b403"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":22,"english":"Hearing the words of Rāvaņa Bali said, \"He is the lord Hari, Nārāyana the protector of the three worlds. He is Ananta,' Kapila-Jisnu' and the highly effulgent Manlion. He is Kratudhămas Sudhāman and has the dreadful mace in his hand. He is like to the twelve Adityas, Purāna and the excellent Puruşa; he is like to the red clouds, the lord of gods and the best god. 1. Lit, etermal endless. Here it is the name of Visnu. 2. A celebrated Muni or saint, the founder of the Sāṁkhya system of philosophy; the son of Kardama by Devahuti and according to some an incarnation of Visnu. 3. Lit-victorious, or triumphant, aname of Visnu. 4. Narasinha-a name of Visnu. When sprayed for by Prahlada to appear from a pillar Vişnu came out in the shape of man-lion and slew Hiranyakaśipu— the king of Daityas and father of Prahlada. 5. Protector of sacrifices-a name of Visnu. 6. Here it is evidently one of the names of Vişņu. In Visnu Purana. Book I, Chap. X. we find another account, Vireyas, married to Gauri, had Sudaman, a Lokapāla, or ruler of the east quarter, as his son.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.447,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-71"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ffea0c56a993d9005ec81070fa305b1ca49f5d2b7a3b145bb917b00c0371056","compact":"54d7723c970867732e4e4664ac27ed9b890203be46e7e8ff31300184f0579878","nasal":"8c261febf29c97cbf71a0b7a889dfa0ff4c8fc698239df18f9dd414d3221c56b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":23,"english":"Even this is my native might this Räksasa will be no more. Hiranyakasipu, the graceful Namuci, and Sambara, Nişandi and Dhūmaketu and Virocana's offspring Bali, and the Daitya Śambhu that mighty monarchs, Vſtra and Bāņa; and Rājarșis versed in all branches of learnings and Gandharvas, and mighty serpents, and sages, and Pannagas and Yaksas, and swarms of Apsarās and the Earth herself containing vastly oceans and mountains and rivers and trees, at the unrolling of a Yuga all these, O mighty monarch have I brought to dissolution. All these and many more endowed with strength and incapable of being overcome, were at the very sight of me compassed with peril, and what is this ranger of the night?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19fa6c5e2a2d5708b62dc0a6b164181ae4f2cdaf5636c1a6c366ccf4ba77636a","compact":"98ca02d8023f667a41065ed0e13c976162571afa2d24499e452b0a6d88fad916","nasal":"2d5fba3c26534b4bde7cf5c1ee6903bdefd8aedb4897a32b6d8a1b0c57d2bb47"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-24","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":24,"english":"Let me go. O you cognisant of righteousness, I shall slay this one. There is none that, albeit strong, can survive after having been seen by me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022024","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e09164c7fd24a10150fb4d1ae3a4b4dbfd351d51ddb930daecd9f310d01c3408","compact":"522de9fe2cbd3cf3968f950ae1e49c85cbaa2548b8357a9364afbc8063d705f5","nasal":"22355cfcd15bd0afe99985e0651e3edf4dd9e67a6f8bc6a3f04a3f346787e09f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-25","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":25,"english":"Verily this is not mine strength, this might pertain to me by nature. O Time, if seen by me, he won't live for a moment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.403,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022025","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fbbadcfee0a727f79e99eeb27cacad35d71e4faa0bd55fae531ce8934a2ad8a9","compact":"3c4384bdcd51d3494d2d73f5b72172f8f252e8eeeb0f66f3400600f0906172d1","nasal":"2e153848567d6f583bec40858b5c81f458c07223fe53e858bba3e1c6e36cb7d0"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-26","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":26,"english":"Hearing these words of his, the puissant king of righteousness spoke there to death, 'Do you stay. I myself shall slay him.' Then with his eyes reddened that lord, Vaivasvata, wielded with his hand the infallible dart of time; while by him lay the redoubtable noose of time and the mace in its native shape resembling fire and the thunderbolt.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022026","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"853b17a8d3ffad576dee95fb3eb8bdfbf2946b21f5002693ad4b461c57915fc5","compact":"1aa685c9fa9a8708a0e2fc13394e4328e960056672e990c74fbc2df4f92f740f","nasal":"1aa685c9fa9a8708a0e2fc13394e4328e960056672e990c74fbc2df4f92f740f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-27","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":27,"english":"Hearing these words of his, the puissant king of righteousness spoke there to death, 'Do you stay. I myself shall slay him.' Then with his eyes reddened that lord, Vaivasvata, wielded with his hand the infallible dart of time; while by him lay the redoubtable noose of time and the mace in its native shape resembling fire and the thunderbolt.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022027","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f220563d1dd4e76c9c12793d9461c21806cdae0bf273e4979a8558ae9bcc206c","compact":"0f10b05dfa349118bbac2612563e9b94f08a72d567babb7dc282bb778512f970","nasal":"0367e6c28059f6dfb2124c66050be82b3df879726f6c2ad774f83ea16fe36ee9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-28","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":28,"english":"Hearing these words of his, the puissant king of righteousness spoke there to death, 'Do you stay. I myself shall slay him.' Then with his eyes reddened that lord, Vaivasvata, wielded with his hand the infallible dart of time; while by him lay the redoubtable noose of time and the mace in its native shape resembling fire and the thunderbolt.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.649,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022028","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f65138630e3eff73d82017afe1f1a68f891ef61fc4a7f13046d2eaa800b97d57","compact":"a74754a7986673145c9f853890548ddcc6e8a8a010a0233951e12c897b76b1a2","nasal":"a74754a7986673145c9f853890548ddcc6e8a8a010a0233951e12c897b76b1a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-29","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":29,"english":"He, who by his very sight draw away the lives of creatures, what should be said of its touching and being hurled at people?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022029","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b40bf158c7c5c83ec2ad7891ac33a0185213ead4f12b6970393d9b84f1bd2cca","compact":"df943819c3d7c28d70b4d834cd2db9a5d85e9601d3e38b4a0beeb52656b64303","nasal":"df943819c3d7c28d70b4d834cd2db9a5d85e9601d3e38b4a0beeb52656b64303"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":30,"english":"And touched by that powerful one, that mighty weapon, engist with flames, attained access of energy, and seemed to consume the Raksasa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.258,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022030","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89d4e0a2b1b1ceb035d320db2f81fc25e725ba908d367ce7295ae6f16dbfd6cd","compact":"bdb986c94bb72936fa98d1dc050245201abb8fa46158fa0493779270dfa148d8","nasal":"104fbe149746866d7d5561d5e5fd7b172c9b34a2b004d4f33159ba55aebf24fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-31","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":31,"english":"In the field of battle, everyone afficted with fear, ran away from it. And beholding Yama with his rod uplifted, the celestials were agitated.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.364,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022031","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28b86c5f682ae39ca06f53390f8e49f2a17170d6b4cfc8061244442e28deb59e","compact":"8850bc9d18e534104efa7bf4513bc492df514f45a9caecfcd3a5016fe74fa1c7","nasal":"fe77cdc5bedb0026c62c84d8b89df9271cc55928cd927ad1caae6526c6214e20"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-32","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":32,"english":"On Yama being desirous of slaying Rāvana, by his rod, the great-father manifesting himself spoke to Yama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022032","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f22db6649b1374bff7ae676fdc21bce567006f9bd7eb48ab3ee09bfabbf6d2de","compact":"27f5c13fa5e35d813b680e4a877a485f37bdb8a8b6c1e2adf9862b6999db8573","nasal":"c33a063e5bd9ce410bc871df2a278aa48c3ce69fd45b9f690a9f7f998bffe820"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-33","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":33,"english":"O Vaivasvata, O mighty-armed one, O you of immeasurable prowess, this certainly must not be. You should not with your rod slay the nightranger.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.317,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022033","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0527ad2578dcbb4f25e0eb25d967d782bc1f1ec82fde69c4fb21b7c6b6b8df4","compact":"e49689ebdb33472d1587d52d591a1851e11da698b8bade802a036ea9192f7f41","nasal":"a32d85c2dcf57002b0fae2ecf9094abe3374df8b2b36a514cad3b00d9cc490ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-34","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":34,"english":"For, O foremost of celestials, I have conferred a boon on him; and you should not render false the words that I have uttered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.25,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022034","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21eb1ada3e9be0920fbd794e14e78ab8dd86b4b4f9e4de1576d0eb593d983ab2","compact":"57b224e712ca71e8a3b565a0c0d48416466af9f70fca4bad2afaaca9ff166087","nasal":"57b224e712ca71e8a3b565a0c0d48416466af9f70fca4bad2afaaca9ff166087"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-35","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":35,"english":"This rod of Kāla, of immeasurable might and incapable of being resisted by creatures, was created by me as having the power of compassing th : death of all beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022035","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f36bb7f400730ed1a7f5c3c7b88baaf073e2962b254b9b12b92f3b2df9853110","compact":"f04753f7b5f3717d6888945dabc178c2de91e5da2de847a08e63ffdf721c15f1","nasal":"4f2f325eb49d89c86fec800f93614ef98c09009b2a4a20ccbf6891ad10a157b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-36","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":36,"english":"Therefore, O mild one, you forsooth should not bring it down on Rāvana's head. If this alights on any one, he does not live for a moment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022036","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29ebca88dd5e7aebbf046bb73300117f4ae0dd8f7b8e9a706b57d8519cf228cc","compact":"a4eac71ae637125a651d6445573e88c82df007e55b8b700bcb722e1242fdea51","nasal":"86a941bb9662fa1f134e5d374002526c66958aa19c7ac1a70bcb32d41877554c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-37","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":37,"english":"Whether on this weapon alighting, the tennecked does not die, or if he does do either way falsehood is the consequence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.651,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022037","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a05631cbe2fbaa08f897b44cd2de24cca501b03d6e980aa846e2732c19b5d900","compact":"a0852d8666c96b845167fbc08fb41011bbf429e77b529658b022a4864449e54a","nasal":"1b2fc53b0f496d8c1e163dd41684f2825961c931432ea8bf9f7b58ff8cedd4ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-38","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":38,"english":"After Närada had reached there, the illustrious Daśānana went to that insular continent beyond even the reach of the celestials. Being struck by the radiant heat of that insular continent, the Puspaka car, of the mighty Ravana, could not stand, there like clouds scattered by the wind. Having arrived at that dreadful insular continent the councillors of the lord of Raksasas, fearfully said to Ravana. \"O lord, we are all stupified and beside ourselves with fear. We cannot anyhow stand here: how shall we fight?” Saying this the Rakşasas fled away into all directions. And Daśānana too sent away his golden car Puşpaka with them. And Daśānana too sent away his chariot and assuming a dreadful figure he alone entered Śvetadvīpa. At the time of his entering he was seen by the females there. One of them of his entering he was seen by the females there. One of them beholding him by the hand and smiling said \"Why have you come hither? Who are you? who is your father? and what for have you come here? Do you definitely say.\" Hearing those words, oking, Ravana, in anger said:-\"I am the son of the ascetic Visrava, I am Ravana by name; I have come hither being desirous of fighting; but I do not behold anyone here.” The vicious-souled Rāvana having said this all the young damsels laughed gently.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.137,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-37-55"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022038","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b64a7d24a059850f4eb17e31c82c4bc37ee88ef8b2af18aac5cef6277cb5afb9","compact":"9b5afa274ff3cbc74f730943b1928c1558c1a63280bc9a083e16d8257b0e7846","nasal":"cb4bfc2f4c49c8b3a38e84e1c0f16fa7fdb5a07454941fa46f6ca014f223a7d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-39","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":39,"english":"Thus addressed, Yama then answered, I restrain this rod. You are our lord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022039","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"99d22928d5ab52b6ade4dafafeadee8a4dd28b63527ab21fbd304ba03e70d0db","compact":"404f05b10a68f68b90d3bf55cd1d76a6b0f1938ad48b52eeff8a963820d830d9","nasal":"a6f18fe3441fed47f0096eb102832f0a092b9eef876402a937fbd2b17d975aad"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-40","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":40,"english":"But as I can not slay this one, who has obtained a boon, what then shall I do now in the field?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.311,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022040","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d62687404bc13841864eaccb258d5ef11be52fde3cbaec442d877cd0e097a945","compact":"b91542487c16bf446f2a78bd864e4a54be2f8cbd9874f5c993e04a44406b7b10","nasal":"8bf8ce8e0b0d38dc71f28fe228078bf94ead2df82745cc036ee1b84ffc5038c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-41","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":41,"english":"Therefore shall I disappear from the sight of this Rākşasa.' Having said this, even there did he vanish with his car and horses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022041","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"061bdd08e3328ca0ac722c7b11165f6f093c76eee2a7ef97d0054e147076c03c","compact":"954d95e71dd0d9bdc7c2f49b2c02a7d46d1f7ac38872599f00689d3b54e85958","nasal":"d4f87d8b116ce78f5f5e697064404574d6d8b4fb3ec6a220b39f47dc463b536c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-42","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":42,"english":"Having vanquished him and distinguished his name, Rāvaņa again ascended his Puşpaka and went out of the abode of Yama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.657,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022042","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06e8aa015d1b02642cb8df217eb2a2e722c3a3d89e51ce3fcd4b9119c58ff9bf","compact":"31a4b39af225cffe8db601ab773eccadbc45ca36251fe708e3c277a647debfb6","nasal":"f91809a3f9da5b8d8d405efa906f5bac468347ac99ef47aecd0ffc146f9a69ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-22-43","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":22,"verse":43,"english":"With a delighted heart Vaivasvata along with the deities headed by Brahmā as well as that mighty ascetic-Narada, went to the celestial regions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.948,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-22-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7022043","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb18d68715274f3ee960fe46efe43b70a18924e20886641c9c7b823c02f0f7e8","compact":"6c23a21fc3500de2ccc6638f8080c9e62d00f083f5efea4b9d347d90ecc56e8b","nasal":"6c23a21fc3500de2ccc6638f8080c9e62d00f083f5efea4b9d347d90ecc56e8b"}}]
